---
import Charter from "../../layouts/Charter.astro";
import Article from "../../components/Article.astro";
import raidHall from "../../../assets/rooms/raid-hall.webp";

const articles = [
  { id: "upcoming", title: "Upcoming raids" },
  { id: "signup", title: "How to sign up" },
  { id: "two-kinds", title: "Two kinds of raid night" },
  { id: "loot", title: "Loot: progression (EPGP)" },
  { id: "casual-loot", title: "Loot: casual and alt nights" },
  { id: "alts", title: "Alts" },
  { id: "attendance", title: "Attendance and guild EP" },
  { id: "chart", title: "The raid chart" },
  { id: "before-pull", title: "Before the pull" },
  { id: "faq", title: "FAQ" },
];
---

<Charter
  title="Raiding · SideQuest"
  description="How raiding works at SideQuest: signing up, the two kinds of raid night, EPGP loot for progression, attendance and guild EP, the raid chart, and what to bring to the pull."
  heading="RAIDING"
  lede="How raid nights work, from signing up to the loot you walk away with."
  art={raidHall}
  artPosition="50% 55%"
  current="raids"
  chamberTitle="How Raiding Works"
  articles={articles}
>
  <script is:inline slot="head">
    const link = document.createElement("link");
    Object.assign(link, {
      rel: "preload",
      as: "fetch",
      href: "/api/events?when=upcoming&kind=raid",
      crossOrigin: "anonymous",
    });
    document.head.append(link);
  </script>

  <Article id="upcoming" n={1} title="Upcoming raids">
    <ul class="quest-log" id="raids-upcoming" aria-live="polite"></ul>
    <p class="chamber-note aside" id="raids-signup-hint">
      Sign in with Discord on the <a href="/account/">account page</a> to see rosters and sign up.
    </p>
    <noscript>
      <p class="aside">Enable JavaScript to see the upcoming raid schedule here, or check the Discord.</p>
    </noscript>
  </Article>

  <Article id="signup" n={2} title="How to sign up">
    <p>You can sign up for a raid two ways:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        On the raid's own page on the site: click through from the <a href="/raids/#upcoming">upcoming list</a> above or
        the <a href="/events/?kind=raid">events page</a> and set your status.
      </li>
      <li>With the Going / Maybe / Can't buttons on the raid's post in the Discord events forum.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Raids need your character, class and role when you sign up. If your plans change, switch to Can't so your spot can
      be filled.
    </p>
    <p>
      Planning to be away? Add the dates on your <a href="/account/">account page</a> and you'll get the Away on a Quest
      role; officers can see who's away right on the raid's event page.
    </p>
    <p>
      Once you're signed up, a private calendar link on your <a href="/account/">account page</a> puts your events and
      sign-ups into Google or Apple Calendar.
    </p>
  </Article>

  <Article id="two-kinds" n={3} title="Two kinds of raid night">
    <p>
      SideQuest raids in two ways: semi-core nights on a set schedule, open to the guild, and a progression group for
      the hardest content. No raid nights are scheduled yet — they go up once enough members have leveled, here and in
      the Discord.
    </p>
    <p>
      How loot works depends on which kind of night you're on: progression raids run on EPGP, casual and alt raids run
      on soft reserve. See below for both.
    </p>
  </Article>

  <Article id="loot" n={4} title="Loot: progression (EPGP)">
    <p>Progression raids use EPGP. Your loot priority is your EP divided by your GP: higher is first in line.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <b>EP</b> (effort points) comes from time in the raid — including wipes on progression bosses — and from time on
        the bench while you're ready to come in.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>GP</b> (gear points) is added when you take an item, from published price bands with named exceptions. Item
        level alone doesn't set the price.
      </li>
      <li>Among everyone who needs an item for their main spec, the highest priority wins it.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You have one EPGP balance per person, per progression team, shared by your main and your alts. Switching
      characters never resets your GP or counts the same raid time twice. Separate progression teams keep separate
      ledgers.
    </p>
    <p>
      Officers record every award and correction with a reason, in game. Corrections keep their history instead of
      erasing it. The site shows the standings.
    </p>
    <p class="chamber-note aside">
      Not set yet: price bands, decay, base and minimum GP, minimum EP, starting balances, ties and trial eligibility,
      and how a balance moves if you transfer teams. These numbers will be posted on this page before the first
      progression raid.
    </p>
  </Article>

  <Article id="casual-loot" n={5} title="Loot: casual and alt nights">
    <p>
      Casual and alt raids run on soft reserve, not EPGP: reserve the item you want before the raid, and reserved items
      go to the people who reserved them. Everything else goes main spec over off spec. These raids never change your
      EPGP balance.
    </p>
    <p class="chamber-note aside">
      Reserve count, lock time and tie rules will be posted here before the first casual raid.
    </p>
  </Article>

  <Article id="alts" n={6} title="Alts">
    <p>
      Your alts share your EPGP balance with your main on the same progression team — playing an alt there doesn't start
      you over, and it doesn't double-count time either. Casual and alt raids don't touch EPGP at all, so there's
      nothing to protect by bringing an alt to one.
    </p>
  </Article>

  <Article id="attendance" n={7} title="Attendance and guild EP">
    <p>This is a different point system from the EPGP above, so don't mix them up:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <b>EPGP</b> decides loot priority on progression raids, per progression team.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Guild EP</b>, shown on the <a href="/heroes/">Hall of Heroes</a>, is earned for attending any guild event,
        whatever kind it is: a raid is worth 10, a dungeon 5, leveling 3, PvP 3, a social night 2, transmog 2, and
        anything else 2. Officers can set a different value for a specific event. It feeds the Hall of Heroes
        leaderboard and badges, not your loot priority.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      For attendance itself: officers mark who came, and the bot counts the minutes you spent in the guild's voice
      channels during the event — 30 minutes or more pre-ticks "came" for an officer to confirm. If attendance isn't
      taken for an event, a "Going" sign-up counts as attended.
    </p>
  </Article>

  <Article id="chart" n={8} title="The raid chart">
    <p>
      Officers place everyone who's signed up into groups 1 through 8, or the bench, right on the raid's event page,
      starting from a suggested balanced layout. Check the chart before the pull — you may not be in the group you
      expect.
    </p>
  </Article>

  <Article id="before-pull" n={9} title="Before the pull">
    <p>Show up ready:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>On time.</li>
      <li>Repaired.</li>
      <li>Stocked on consumables.</li>
      <li>
        Running the addons the group asked for — see the <a href="/addons/">addons page</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Article>

  <Article id="faq" n={10} title="FAQ">
    <p>
      <b>I can't make a raid I signed up for. What do I do?</b>
    </p>
    <p>
      Switch your status to Can't as soon as you know, on the raid's page or in the Discord, so your spot can be filled.
    </p>

    <p>
      <b>What does it mean if I'm on the bench?</b>
    </p>
    <p>
      You're signed up and ready to come in. Time on the bench while you're ready still earns EPGP on progression
      nights.
    </p>

    <p>
      <b>Do I need the raid addon to raid?</b>
    </p>
    <p>No. Nobody needs it to raid — it just adds convenience.</p>

    <p>
      <b>Can I bring an alt to progression night?</b>
    </p>
    <p>
      Yes, and it shares your EPGP balance with your main on that team, so you're never starting over or losing credit
      for showing up.
    </p>

    <p>
      <b>Where do I see my EPGP standing?</b>
    </p>
    <p>Officers keep the points in game, and the standings will show here once progression raids start.</p>

    <p>
      <b>Where do I see my guild EP?</b>
    </p>
    <p>
      On the <a href="/heroes/">Hall of Heroes</a>, alongside your badges.
    </p>

    <p>
      <b>What does Maybe mean when I sign up?</b>
    </p>
    <p>You're not committed either way yet. Switch to Going or Can't once you know, so officers can plan around it.</p>

    <p>
      <b>How is attendance decided if I didn't get marked?</b>
    </p>
    <p>
      The bot counts your voice-channel minutes during the event; 30 minutes or more pre-ticks "came" for an officer to
      confirm. If the event's attendance was never taken, your "Going" sign-up counts as attended on its own.
    </p>

    <p>
      <b>Do casual and alt raids use EPGP?</b>
    </p>
    <p>No. They run on soft reserve and never change your EPGP balance.</p>

    <p>
      <b>Who decides the raid chart?</b>
    </p>
    <p>
      Officers do, starting from a suggested balanced layout and placing everyone into groups 1-8 or the bench on the
      event page.
    </p>
  </Article>
</Charter>

<script>
  import {
    apiFetch,
    fetchMe,
    onFreshData,
    escapeHtml,
    requireElement,
    statusMessage,
    type EventSummary,
  } from "../../scripts/api";
  import { onPage } from "../../scripts/page";
  import { weekdayPhrase } from "../../scripts/series";

  const RAIDS_PATH = "/api/events?when=upcoming&kind=raid";

  // Quest-giver marks: a gold "!" for an event still open to sign-ups, a dim "?" once it has run.
  function questMark(event: EventSummary): string {
    const open = event.status === "scheduled" && new Date(event.starts_at).getTime() > Date.now();
    return `<svg class="ico ico-quest${open ? "" : " is-done"}" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#${open ? "i-quest" : "i-quest-done"}"></use></svg>`;
  }

  onPage("#raids-upcoming", () => {
    // Only signed-out visitors need telling how to sign up.
    fetchMe().then(
      () => requireElement("raids-signup-hint").setAttribute("hidden", ""),
      () => undefined,
    );

    const dayFormat = new Intl.DateTimeFormat(undefined, { weekday: "short", month: "short", day: "numeric" });
    const timeFormat = new Intl.DateTimeFormat(undefined, { hour: "numeric", minute: "2-digit" });

    function raidRow(event: EventSummary): string {
      const start = new Date(event.starts_at);
      const counts = (() => {
        if (!event.counts) {
          return "";
        }
        const signupCounts = `${event.counts.tank}T · ${event.counts.healer}H · ${event.counts.dps}D${
          event.counts.tentative > 0 ? ` · ${event.counts.tentative} tentative` : ""
        }`;
        return event.counts.interested > 0
          ? `${signupCounts} · ${event.counts.interested} interested on Discord`
          : signupCounts;
      })();
      const statusSuffix =
        event.status === "scheduled" ? "" : ` · ${event.status === "cancelled" ? "Cancelled" : "Completed"}`;
      const seriesText = event.series ? weekdayPhrase(event.series.weekdays, event.series.interval_weeks) : "";
      const meta = [event.location, seriesText, counts].filter(Boolean).join(" · ");
      return `
      <li>
        <a class="quest" href="/events/detail/?id=${event.id}">
          ${questMark(event)}
          <span>
            <span class="quest-name">${escapeHtml(event.title)}${escapeHtml(statusSuffix)}</span>
            <span class="quest-meta">${escapeHtml(meta)}</span>
          </span>
          <span class="quest-when">${escapeHtml(timeFormat.format(start))}<small>${escapeHtml(dayFormat.format(start))}</small></span>
        </a>
      </li>`;
    }

    async function loadRaids(): Promise<void> {
      const list = requireElement("raids-upcoming");
      try {
        const raids = await apiFetch<EventSummary[]>(RAIDS_PATH);
        list.innerHTML =
          raids.length > 0
            ? raids.map(raidRow).join("")
            : `<li class="quest-empty">Nothing scheduled yet. Raid nights go up once enough members have leveled — check back here or in the Discord, and add the <a href="/account/">calendar link</a> so you don't miss the post.</li>`;
      } catch (err) {
        list.innerHTML = `<li class="quest-empty">${escapeHtml(statusMessage(err))}</li>`;
      }
    }

    onFreshData(RAIDS_PATH, () => void loadRaids());
    void loadRaids();
  });
</script>
